75210381"},{"analysis":"This overview duplicates inline:4234741655. The shared API Gateway extractor now emits sanitized URL_QUERY when query parameters are available; default redaction and query-bearing exact library and installed-agent assertions pass.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"review:5475576707"},{"analysis":"Confirmed against the factory's explicit v1.44.0 schema and released HTTP server convention. Extract the existing encoded query once and emit URL_QUERY through UrlQuerySanitizer.redactQueryString with the same sensitiveQueryParameters used by URL_FULL. Tests verify default/configured redaction, encoding, omission for null/empty queries, wrapper a=b&c=d, and installed-agent q=value&sig=REDACTED.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"inline:4234741655"}],"input_identity":{},"outcome":"fixes","proposal":{"body":"<!--\nCHANGELOG.md is generated from merged pull requests. Do not add an entry unless this PR introduces\na deprecation or breaking change.\n-->\n\nAdd scope schema URL v1.44.0 to AWS Lambda invocation and API Gateway telemetry so backends can identify the emitted semantic conventions.\n\nAPI Gateway spans also emit `url.path`, `url.scheme`, `http.route`, and sanitized `url.query` when available. Invocation exception logs carry the schema URL; SQS schema selection is unchanged.\n\nThe `cloud.resource_id` alias-to-version ARN change is split into #20493 for separate review. This PR preserves the invoked ARN as the resource ID.\n\nAWS Lambda only; GenAI and generic JMX remain outside this PR.\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX -->\n\n- Related to #11939","title":"Emit AWS Lambda schema URLs and API Gateway HTTP attributes"},"request_digest":"83b07cbee8f1661997d63806b799747786e0bdd4fdfdd40c5baadb3d8e2e2b00","schema":2},"download_sha256":"fd41af859e773499fc3a0cfc5b2475b2253e248226228ecb9aa60bf263017b07","frozen_sha":"7759e9ce35eaf19915ca08336a92af57a7988e5e","pr":20483,"publication_eligible":false,"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetr