en finding</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Emit sanitized URL_QUERY when the request contains query parameters](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20483#discussion_r4234741655) \u00b7 New\n</details>\n\n\ud83e\udde0 **Review effort:** Balanced","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5475576707","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5475576707},{"body":"[General] The v1.44 HTTP server convention makes `url.query` conditionally required whenever a query was received. This extractor already receives `request.getQueryStringParameters()` (and the updated wrapper test sends `a=b&c=d`), but the new v1.44 attribute set still exposes that query only inside `url.full`; `url.full` is not a substitute for `url.query`. Please emit a sanitized `URL_QUERY` using the same sensitive-parameter configuration and cover it in the query-bearing assertions.","comment_commit_id":"7759e9ce35eaf19915ca08336a92af57a7988e5e","comment_id":4234741655,"key":"inline:4234741655","kind":"inline","line":76,"original_commit_id":"7759e9ce35eaf19915ca08336a92af57a7988e5e","original_line":76,"path":"instrumentation/aws-lambda/aws-lambda-events-common-2.2/library/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/instrumentation/awslambdaevents/common/v2_2/internal/ApiGatewayProxyAttributesExtractor.java","review_commit_id":"7759e9ce35eaf19915ca08336a92af57a7988e5e","review_id":5475576707,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-09T21:36:03Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"